t of left  or right wing content but of independent  content which is I believe being  deprioritized in lieu of corporate news  channels we are getting absolutely  crushed on YouTube as a result of the  algorithmic changes that have gone on  now I can't  say if this is because of one thing or  another what I can tell you is that this  predates the steven crowder Carlos Mazda  Fiasco it may have been exacerbated by  that but this is bigger than that and  it's really just genuinely bad for our  channel to make money on YouTube you  need views and the views need to be  monetized meaning it's not just views  but the views need to have ads play  before them in order for us to make  money now there are a bunch of different  ways that we get views on YouTube one  big way is called browse features browse  features include we have close to  700,000 subscribers on YouTube when  those people see our videos on their  homepage under their list of  subscriptions that is called a browse  feature view if someone views our  channel through something like that it's  mostly a function of subscribers the  more subscribers you have the more  Browse feature views you are going to  get there's another one which is called  suggested videos which are those videos  that YouTube suggests alongside on  desktop or below on mobile the video  that you are watching and this is a  hugely variable source of views and it  is dependent on YouTube's algorithmic  priorities our portion of views that  come from this suggested video feed has  declined by about 50%  back in September about 33% of our views  were coming from the suggested view  suggested features a sort of umbrella  that number has dropped from 33% to  under 17% and I'll explain to you why  this is such a big deal this is about  half of what we were once getting from  this algorithm and this decline started  right after YouTube announced that in an  effort to crack down on fake news it  will be doing more backing as they say  of what they call authoritative sources  and of course what might be a  well-intentioned good-faith effort to  crack down on fake news appears to be  absolutely crushing independent  producers  like us this decline from 33% to 17% of  our views coming from YouTube suggested  videos feed is a huge blow to our  revenue because it represents a ton of  views we had three and a half million  views in December not on the entire  channel just from the suggested video  feed okay in June we'll be lucky to get  one and a half million views from the  suggested video feed that's a two  million view shortfall okay that's a  huge revenue shortfall now I have to be  careful because my understanding is that  YouTube's Terms and Conditions say I  can't give you specific revenue numbers  so I'm not going to but losing two  million views because of changes to  YouTube's algorithm is a lot more money  than most people in the audience would  guess okay let me put it that way  and in the meantime although YouTube is  claiming that they're putting in place a  better more efficient system to make  sure the videos that are brand safe do  get ads playing on them look at what  happened yesterday we had a video from  yesterday get 90,000 views in the first  four hours a very this is in the top 1%  of our videos by getting 90,000 views  and in just the first four hours this  was a video about Donald Trump's  interview with George Stephanopoulos  where they talked about Donald Trump's  finances and the video was instantly  demonetised as you can see from the  yellow dollar sign on the screen  monetized videos have a green dollar  sign there is nothing not brand safe in  this video we appealed the decision were  told that those decisions should be  reviewed within an hour and it was not  reviewed for about 14 hours until such  time that the video had a hundred and  ten thousand views it has now been  romana ties but we lost the revenue on  one hundred and ten thousand views so  listen I have no control about over this  I have no control over any of what's  going on here channels like ours are  uniquely positioned to be the most  damaged from these algorithmic changes  and I'll explain what I mean by that the  big corporate news channel CNN whoever  they have huge ad revenue  outside of YouTube and YouTube is  favoring them anyway so they're fine  really small channels don't depend on  YouTube to fund ongoing multi employee  operations they're fine we who are in  the top one-and-a-half percent of  YouTube but not in the top point one  percent we are the people who will most  suffer so what can we do  I've said it before and I'll say it  again we've got two separate funding  from advertising that's it okay we have  direct support set up on our website  where we get 98% of every payment okay  we pay a two percent payment processing  fee ninety-eight percent of the  contributions through membership on our  website go directly to funding the show  we're looking at launching channels in  other languages with our content dubbed  in very high quality to reach people who  don't speak English we've started paying  for the subtitling and closed captioning  of our channel already we produce and  give the show to 200 non-commercial  radio and TV stations all of that stuff  costs money and under one percent of our  audience funds us directly through  membership right now if we can get to  two percent of our audience funding us  directly we laugh about these YouTube  issues we'll be in great shape if we can  get to three percent of our audience  funding us directly we would be  absolutely crushing it so this has to be  a wake-up call okay we've got to support  the shows that we value directly if we  can afford to do so if you can't that's  okay I'm still doing the show for you  okay I don't need your last dollar but  if you're used to buying one of those  lattes or two a month consider going to  WWJ pakman.com and saying I can afford  three bucks a month I can afford six  bucks a month the coupon code this is  2020 will save you 40% we're not talking  about a lot of money if you apply that  code to the $6 a month membership it's  three dollars and sixty cents a month  okay if you apply that coupon code to  the yearly membership it'll drop it from  $60 to just $36 let's make this happen  because this is this it's not any more  about this could happen  this is happening we have lost half of  our views on YouTube from the suggested  video feed and increasingly we  recommended the suggested videos our  corporate establishment legacy media  let's make this happen  okay I truly believe that our audience  is going to understand the importance of  this and I look forward to coming back  to you in a week and telling you how  inspired and flattered I am from the  audience support

